WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.010
- So, let me know if this
has ever happened to you.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:04.950
You get really excited
about starting a new diet.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.150
You're starting to feel
like crap about yourself

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.670
and you think a new diet
will solve all your problems.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.810
So you start doing some research online.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.180
You read one article about the keto diet

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.560
and how it's changing millions of lives.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.010
And then you read another article

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.420
about how the paleo diet is the way to go.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.180
And then you keep on
going down the rabbit hole

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.230
and you get into veganism and you get into

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.990
the carnivore diet which is
completely a 180 from veganism.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.070
Something tells me people
on the carnivore diet

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.540
don't hate vegans, but
vegans really hate people

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:33.530
on the carnivore diet.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.550
But anyways, this kind of
situation often happened to me,

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.453
but more about starting a business.

00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:41.080
Back in university I was
pretty stressed about

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.790
making my tuition payments
and I was really frustrated

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.091
with my financial situation.

00:00:45.091 --> 00:00:47.140
So I would often look online

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.740
for best online businesses
to start in 2019.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.030
And I'd read articles
about how drop shipping

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.760
will make you millions of dollars.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.180
Then I would watch another video talking

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.840
about how drop shipping is
dead and you missed the boat.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.180
So you should start your
own digital marketing agency

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.080
or something like that.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.560
The point I'm trying to make is that

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.330
we live in the information age.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.961
And this is supposed to mean
that we have an abundance

00:01:08.961 --> 00:01:12.320
of knowledge and no
matter what we want to do,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.670
we can learn how to do it.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.540
We can be whatever we want to be

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.480
and we can learn how to be that thing,

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.330
usually for free, online,
using the internet.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.100
While this is technically true,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.090
we do have this unique problem.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.230
There is so much information out there.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:29.700
So many people telling you
what the right thing to do is,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.754
that it often contradicts other people.

00:01:31.754 --> 00:01:33.319
And it all just becomes a wash.

00:01:33.319 --> 00:01:36.140
We're kind of paralyzed by
the amount of information,

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.330
not really knowing what path to take.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.530
Being someone who spends so
much time on the internet,

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.530
this was especially a problem for me.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.770
But luckily I've adopted a
mindset that really helps me

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.360
cut through the crap and
just get on with my life.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.800
I'm finding it's my preferred philosophy

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.220
for life in general.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.520
And this philosophy or mindset,

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.240
I call the Shoot-First Mentality.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.530
Rather than obsessively deliberating

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.470
over what path to take,
just start walking one.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.200
Making bold, uncalculated decisions,

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.460
firing from the hip, is often the antidote

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.340
to this endless deliberation.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.340
If you make bold, courageous,
decisions at the drop of a hat

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.520
and make this your default
mode of solving problems

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.420
just trying something,
noticing it doesn't work,

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.400
trying again, revising.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.530
Having this action first policy can offer

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.460
a plethora of benefits.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.260
Firstly, with an action first mindset

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.210
you can get better at things quicker

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:35.020
than people who are
sitting on the sidelines

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:35.853
reading about it.

00:02:35.853 --> 00:02:38.340
A great example of this is
when I started this channel.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.500
I had been really thinking
about the proper way

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.580
to make a self-improvement channel

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.140
and theorizing about
like, whether there was

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.050
a opening in the market for
me or if it was too saturated

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.560
or how I could make myself stand out.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.530
By the time I made my first video,

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.730
none of that really mattered.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.050
Making my first video presented challenges

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.700
that I never knew I would have.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.920
And I was able to improve upon
them with every single video.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.433
And I think it's two or
three years later, here I am.

00:03:04.433 --> 00:03:06.200
Things are going very well.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.140
And I've learned a lot along the way.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.640
Getting your hands dirty, making mistakes,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:14.940
trying new things, is by far
the fastest way to learn.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.290
It's way faster than reading about it.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.040
By watching videos about it.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.100
Actually being in the act of doing

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.440
the thing that you want
to do and failing at it

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.680
will make you get better,
faster than anything else.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.340
The second benefit of adopting
an action first mindset

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.840
is that it hardens you.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:35.270
Or as David Goggins would
say, "It calluses your mind."

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.970
And this is all about
getting used to discomfort.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.990
If you train yourself to
battle past the discomfort

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.140
of taking immediate, acute action,

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.260
then you're able to embrace that feeling.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.180
You're able to push past the
resistance holding you back

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.950
from doing what's right,
rather than what's comfortable.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.220
This makes you a very strong
and capable individual.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.380
In times of crisis where
people are losing their heads

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.750
because something really
tragic is happening

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.660
and something uncomfortable
but necessary needs to be done,

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.790
you'll be the kind of
person who can stand there

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:07.580
and do that type of thing
because you're an action taker.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.130
You're not somebody who worries
and stays in their head.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.840
You look for the opportunity
to take the necessary action

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.060
and you execute on it.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.747
Ralph Waldo Emerson has this great quote.

00:04:16.747 --> 00:04:18.930
"Do the thing and you
will have the power."

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.410
It's hilarious quote
because it's so simple,

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.430
but it's also a very popular quote

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.260
because it's so simply true.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.220
It's really good at describing
the one-to-one relationship

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.480
between action and results.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.550
Nothing else will move
anything other than action.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:36.720
Thinking about it, theorizing
about it, worrying about it,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.880
fantasizing about it.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.760
Nothing changes anything
except taking action.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.850
Do the thing and you will have the power.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.610
Another reason why having
an action first mindset

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:48.140
is superior to a planning first mindset

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.950
is because with an action first mindset

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.120
you're gonna get burned.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.170
But the lessons you
learned by getting burned

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:55.460
are the ones you remember.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:56.988
So I have a pretty funny story about this.

00:04:56.988 --> 00:04:59.970
We're told our whole life
that gossiping is bad.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.300
Don't talk about other
people behind their backs.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.960
You know, don't talk (beep), basically.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.970
I was also told this my whole life.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.320
The reason why I didn't really register,

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.160
I just knew it was bad. Don't do it.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.600
But fast forward to when I was about 16.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.880
There I was at a social outing

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.420
and I started going off about how stupid

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.880
some lady's outfit was that I saw.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.380
And I kept on going on about it,

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.960
just to get attention to myself.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.280
I was hoping to get a
few laughs, ridiculing

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.730
this one lady's outfit that
we could all relate to.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.330
And after going on about
it for like, I don't know,

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.160
30 whole seconds, I realized that

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.100
no one's really laughing at all.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.050
In fact, they look pretty uncomfortable.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.750
And that was because sure enough,

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.780
that lady's daughter was one
of the girls I was talking to.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.520
It was one of the most
devastating moments of my life.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.530
My heart completely sank.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.410
I turned into a shell of a human being.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:52.800
Definitely top three most
embarrassing moments of my life.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.800
And I can guarantee you I
never made that mistake again.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.850
But do I regret it? I don't.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.110
Because I was firing from the hip.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.920
I got burned and I'm a
better person because of it.

